/*
 * NON_MATCHING: ovl_14_02's game object, complete; not in the ROM.
 * flags: -O3
 * differing words: us 1353, eu 1353, jp 1353
 *
 * 120 of 138 functions match (the same in every version). A first draft:
 * m2c output (with the ZeroJump prototypes of the other drafts and the
 * file's own signatures, scratch/newovl4/protos.h and own.h) made to
 * compile; generated by scratch/newovl4/build.sh, with hand-written
 * functions in fx/.
 *
 * jp: only 8004CDE0 differs. jp tests 0x1023(0x1006()) and calls
 * 0x1008(1) right after setting the new object's angles, before the loop
 * that waits for it to rise; us and eu do it after that loop
 * (`#if VERSION_JP`). jp's ZeroJump numbers differ too.
 *
 * Ported from matched C: 80043010 (ovl_13_01's 80043F88), 80043358
 * (ovl_15_01's 80043010), 80044930, 8004CBE4 (ovl_14_01), 80045348,
 * 8004DE28 and the 0x34-word handlers 80045D88/80045EB4/80047B6C/80047BF4
 * (ovl_13_01, through m2c), 80048830 (ovl_13_02's 80043B64, 35 words
 * left), 8004CCA8 (ovl_15_01's 80043104 with the target read by 0x182B),
 * 8004DF98/8004DFA0 (ovl_13_02's 8004B524/B52C). Tuned by hand to match:
 * 8004314C (8 bytes of pad), 800441AC, 800440C4, 80048E98 (the division
 * written at each use), 8004E138 (D_800502B8 a Vec3f written x, y, z),
 * 8004E4E4 (`case 17`, the inlined 8004DF98). Rewritten from the asm as
 * plain C (pass 2): 800436F0, 80044720 (`d /= 15` before the loop),
 * 80044888, 8004327C (three early `return 1`), 8004B120 (Vec3f literals
 * stored x, y, z), 8004772C (calls 80047704, which IDO then inlines, and
 * that keeps 800471A4/80046BBC out of 80047704), 80047FB4 (a switch),
 * 80044C08 (`n--; goto done;`). 8004D580 is a static (it uses $s0
 * unsaved; not inlined, called four times from 8004D640).
 *
 * Order: every function and stub comes out at the original's place.
 * 8004E624 and 8004E4E4 are defined below 8004E2CC (climb.py). Statics:
 * 800430A8 and 80043890 take their object in $s0; 8004DF98 is a static
 * with a body (ovl_13_02's 8004B524), inlined into 8004DFA0 and 8004E4E4;
 * the stubs 8004D570/78, 8004D628/30/38 and 8004E2AC-8004E2C4 are K&R
 * empty statics inlined into the next function; the 18 at
 * 8004E824-8004E8AC are unused. 8004B604 passes its f32 (in $f12) to the
 * state handlers it switches to.
 *
 * Data: .data defined where its first user puts it (8004FF00-8004FF10
 * above 8004E2CC, the Vec3f[8] table 8004FF14 above 8004CDE0, the
 * counters 8004FF7C-8004FF8C above 8004B7E0); 8004FF74 is 8004BDE8's
 * initialised f32[2] local, 8004FF90 a string literal. .bss defined; the
 * types are partly guesses (Vec3f groups); fillers keep the addresses.
 *
 * Pass 5 rewrote as plain C from the asm (frame layouts read from the
 * spilled homes): 8004CDE0 (matches: `speed = dir[2] / 30` with an int
 * literal, `ang[0] = a - b; ang[0] /= 50.0f;`, a dead `if (!h) {}`),
 * 80046374 (79 words, 4 bytes long: &D_800503F0 reloaded in loop 3),
 * 80044C60 (40 words, right size; f2 for f14), 8004C660 (86 words, right
 * size; the zeroing as chained stores `D_394 = D_3A8 = 0;`), 80046C4C
 * (267 words, frame 0x70 against 0x68).
 *
 * Pass 6 rewrote from the asm: 80045384 (matches: frame read from the
 * spills, `goto loop`, an unused f32[3] below the counter), 800482A0
 * (matches: scalars declared above pos), 800438D4 (185 words, frame 8
 * too big), 80049DE0 (125) and 8004A894 (7) and 8004AD5C (63): in this
 * family of camera-path functions, hi/lo are set after the vectors and
 * the call is `f(..., t -= lo, hi -= lo)`.
 *
 * Pass 7 put the camera-path family (80048EFC .. 8004B230) in one
 * template; pass 8 rewrote 800471EC, 8004338C, 80045AD0, 80049634 and
 * 8004BB3C (match), 80047844 (2 words), 80044980 (17), 8004C240 (106)
 * and 8004B7E0 (122) from the asm. D_800503F0_VEC reads D_800503F0..F8
 * as a Vec3f (the .bss is split there). Pass 9: 80047844 matches (a
 * register-only `i` declared between pos and flag); 80048490 (7) indexes
 * the four fixed entries after the do-while with the loop's `i`, so uopt
 * strength-reduces every D_800502F0[i] to one pointer; 80046C4C (224)
 * holds the A180 difference in a local and the final speed in arg1.
 *
 * Not faithful: 8004AABC's original computes the +40 wrap of the
 * re-read field into a register and then tests the RAW field (the
 * wrapped value is dead); every C form that does that lets uopt delete
 * the wrap, so the draft wraps into lo and tests t = lo instead (76 words,
 * 8 bytes short).
 *
 * What still differs, in large: 80046C4C (FP registers; the original
 * keeps the speed in $f14 where arg1 goes to its home), 800438D4 (frame
 * 8 too big; the original stores the two step vectors to three scalar
 * slots 0x68/0x64/0x60), 8004D640 (registers), 8004C240 (the constant 1
 * shared in $a1). The
 * infinite loops 8004BF90 and 80043E88, and 8004BDE8 before 8004BF90,
 * differ in their trailing alignment nops: their counts move with the
 * sizes of the functions above them.
 */
#include "common.h"

#define M2C_FIELD(expr, type, offset) (*(type)((u8 *)(expr) + (offset)))

#define A180(v) (((v) >= 0.0f && (v) <= 180.0f) ? (v) : (360.0f - (v)) * -1.0f)
#define WRAP360(x) ((x) >= 360.0f ? (x) - 360.0f : ((x) < 0.0f ? (x) + 360.0f : (x)))
#define D_800503F0_VEC (*(Vec3f *) &D_ovl14_02_800503F0)

